#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1d4b0c2-10d0-5c3a-8a58-4d7598dd9f96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Perimeter of a Triangle Given the Perimeter of Another Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "00942425-ab13-5a50-a63a-d29cf2f34889" :question/math-academy-id "e-2752" :question/problem "The perimeter $p_1$ of the triangle $\\triangle{ABC}$ shown below is $21$. What is the perimeter of the triangle $\\triangle{ABD}$ if ${BD}=3$?\n\n![](images/66/66780ce63515be8445234ce991ae64506c6325f04b2aabb0318fb8b86c1bf2d7.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we can see that $\\triangle{ABC}$ is an equilateral triangle.\n\nWe're told that the perimeter of $\\triangle ABC$ is $p_1=21$, and since all $3$ sides have equal length, each side must have a length of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{p_1}{3}= \\dfrac{21}{3} = 7\\,\n$$\n\nSo now we know that\n\n$$\nAB=BC=AC = 7\n$$\n\nand we have enough information to compute the perimeter of the triangle $\\triangle{ABD}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= AB + BD + DA \\\\\n&= 7 + 3 + 7 \\\\\n&= 17\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of $\\triangle ABD$ is $p=17$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f6c0ca1-297a-5f25-bccf-c74d0c565c24" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Perimeter of a Polygon"}] :question/id #uuid "b4864184-6983-58ab-9787-524e04dc5c73" :question/math-academy-id "e-2754" :question/problem "In a pentagon $ABCDE$, the measures of the sides are ${AB} = 25\\,\\mathrm{mm}$, ${BC} = 26\\,\\mathrm{mm}$, ${CD} = 30\\,\\mathrm{mm}$, ${DE} = 18\\,\\mathrm{mm}$, and ${EA} = 21\\,\\mathrm{mm}$.\nWhat is the perimeter of the pentagon?" :question/worked-solution "The perimeter $p$ of a polygon is the sum of the measures of all its sides. So, we can simply calculate\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= 25mm + 26mm + 30mm + 18mm + 21mm \\\\\n&= 120mm\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is a large quantity of $\\textrm{mm}$, we will convert to $\\textrm{cm}$:\n\n$$\np = 120\\, \\mathrm{mm} = 12\\,\\mathrm{cm}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2c2a15f-617d-5515-98a8-ccdc525092b3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of Variables Given Two Isoperimetric Polygons"}] :question/id #uuid "3de76784-4137-5093-9c35-847edd10ef62" :question/math-academy-id "e-2756" :question/problem "A regular pentagon has the same perimeter as an equilateral triangle whose side is $15\\,\\mathrm{cm}$. Find the length of the side of the pentagon." :question/worked-solution "Since all the sides of an equilateral triangle are equal, its perimeter is\n\n$$\np=3\\cdot 15=45\n$$\n\nLet $a$ be the side of the pentagon. We know that our polygons have equal perimeters. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= 5a \\\\\n45 &= 5a \\\\\n9 &= a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the length of the side is $9 \\,\\mathrm{cm}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105806 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1d4b0c2-10d0-5c3a-8a58-4d7598dd9f96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Perimeter of a Triangle Given the Perimeter of Another Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa25d7b1-96fa-52f0-be81-b199d162aff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102699} {:answer/id #uuid "ae67b8ec-458e-55d4-b5a0-2d5265868380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102700} {:answer/id #uuid "01d4e827-5964-5226-ade4-d2fe911613ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102701} {:answer/id #uuid "26f4048a-e58a-5660-9d0c-02d705d513f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102702} {:answer/id #uuid "4b07a6aa-ddb4-5bbb-a063-0274c04df652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102703}] :answer-field/id #uuid "101d66ee-6f45-53d6-9e1f-cb607ea196f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102698}] :question/id #uuid "96a7a6cd-52f8-51e5-9286-b855874bfcac" :question/math-academy-id "q-20568" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4ab3c4ba281be5363c5ea3e2b3fce6aec91221b31a762ef645c7262095866d5e.png)\n\nThe perimeter $p_{1}$ of the triangle $△DBC$ shown above is $10$. What is the perimeter of the triangle $△ABC$ if $BD = 3$?"}]}
